PERFORMANCE & MEMORY IMPROVEMENTS
==================================

Expected improvements from these changes:

1. Parquet Caching:
   - First load: reads CSV, converts categorical dtypes, saves to parquet
   - Subsequent loads: read cached parquet (5-20x faster, 2-5x less memory)
   - Categorical dtypes preserved across loads

2. Reduced Preprocessing Duplication:
   - fraud_detection.py, random_forest.py, decision_tree.py now share DataLoader
   - Eliminates repeated CSV reads and categorical encoding
   - Consistent data pipeline across all scripts

3. Development Workflow:
   - --nrows flag enables quick dev iterations on subsets
   - --rebuild-cache allows explicit cache regeneration
   - Faster test cycles without repeated full-data processing

4. Memory Efficiency:
   - Categorical columns stored as category dtype in parquet
   - Numeric columns filled only after categorical->codes conversion
   - No unnecessary data duplication during preprocessing

CLI USAGE
=========

Rebuild parquet cache from CSVs:
  python3 scripts/project_setup.py --rebuild-cache

Load only first 10,000 rows (dev mode):
  python3 scripts/project_setup.py --nrows 10000

Standard setup:
  python3 scripts/project_setup.py

Create virtual environment:
  python3 -m venv .venv
  source .venv/bin/activate
  pip install -r requirements.txt

TECHNICAL DETAILS
=================

Data Flow:
1. project_setup.py loads CSVs or cached parquet
2. Known categorical columns converted to pandas 'category' dtype
3. Parquet files written with categorical metadata preserved
4. fraud_detection.py, random_forest.py, decision_tree.py prefer cached parquet
5. Lightweight preprocessing (fillna numeric, encode categorical->codes)
6. Consistent feature pipeline across all scripts

Type Handling:
- Categorical columns: stored as category dtype, converted to codes (int) before use
- Numeric columns: fillna(0) applied after categorical conversion
- Object dtype columns: converted to categorical codes on first encounter

Caching Strategy:
- train_clean.parquet and test_clean.parquet stored in data/ folder
- use_parquet=True (default) enables automatic fallback to parquet when available
- use_parquet=False forces CSV reload (useful with --rebuild-cache)

