RECOMMENDATIONS FOR FUTURE WORK
================================

1. Add explicit dtype_map in DataLoader for known column types
   - Further reduce memory usage at CSV read time
   - Pre-define numeric column dtypes (e.g., int32 instead of int64)

2. Implement logging instead of print() statements
   - Adjustable verbosity levels
   - Better output control for batch runs

3. Add unit tests for DataLoader and prepare_data functions
   - Verify parquet roundtrip fidelity
   - Test dtype preservation

4. Consider polars for extremely large CSV files
   - 10-100x faster CSV parsing than pandas
   - Lower memory usage with lazy evaluation

5. Add a .gitignore entry for *_clean.parquet
   - Prevent committing large cached files to repository
   - Allow regeneration via --rebuild-cache

6. Create a simple benchmark script
   - Compare load times: CSV vs parquet
   - Measure memory usage with different dtypes

